{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/pulls/3132","id":5146686740,"node_id":"PR_kwDOHXVlhM8AAAABMsQ1FA","html_url":"https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/pull/3132","diff_url":"https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/pull/3132.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/pull/3132.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/issues/3132","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/pulls/3132/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/pulls/3132/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/issues/3132/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/statuses/e1f207e9e8453a7343a1a72f741225de93673763","number":3132,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[CuTe, SM120] fp8 (e4m3 / e5m2) forward on SM12x","user":{"login":"lucifer1004","id":13583761,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTgzNzYx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13583761?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucifer1004","html_url":"https://github.com/lucifer1004","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucifer1004/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucifer1004/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucifer1004/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucifer1004/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucifer1004/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucifer1004/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucifer1004/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucifer1004/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucifer1004/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Builds on #3109 (which builds on #3108); review those first.** This branch contains their commits; the one commit specific to this PR is the last:\n- `[CuTe, SM120] fp8 (e4m3 / e5m2) forward on SM12x`\n\n## What this does\nFP8 forward for the SM12x kernels of #3109 (RTX PRO Blackwell, GeForce RTX 50xx, DGX Spark / GB10). It follows the SM100 FP8 contract:\n- **Inputs and output:** e4m3 or e5m2 inputs, bf16 O, fp32 LSE.\n- **Descales:** optional `q_descale` / `k_descale` / `v_descale` of shape (batch, num_kv_heads).\n- **Backward:** none. FP8 with `requires_grad` raises, as on SM100.\n\n**Coverage:**\n- **Head dims:** (head_dim, head_dim_v) in 64, 96, 128, 192, 192 / 128 and 256. Other shapes are rejected on the host with the supported list.\n- **Masks and score modifiers:** causal, local, softcap, score_mod / mask_mod, learnable sink, pack_gqa.\n- **Layouts:** varlen Q/K and seqused, paged KV, SplitKV (fixed, and per batch through the scheduler metadata of #3109).\n- **Block sparsity:** dense, paged, and varlen Q over paged caches.\n\n**Shared code** (the defaults leave every existing kernel unchanged):\n- `FlashAttentionForwardBase` carries `o_dtype` for the O SMEM store and gmem copy layout. Its epilogue takes an optional `store_sO` for kernels whose O accumulator is not in the tiled MMA's C layout.\n- The SM80-style `Softmax` takes SM100's `max_offset`: P and the row sum carry `2**max_offset`, which keeps small probabilities of an fp8 P in the e4m3 normal range.\n\n**SM12x kernels** (`sm120/flash_fwd.py`, `sm120/runtime.py`):\n- **PV MMA:** m16n8k32 with both operands fp8, so P is fp8 (scaled by `2**8`). V stays MN-major in SMEM and loads with `ldmatrix` m16n16.trans.b8; there is no V repack.\n- **hd 256:** the split-PV tiles (P through SMEM) with whole 32-key chunks per block. fp8 K/V stages take half the SMEM these tiles were sized for, which leaves room for a second stage with K loaded a block ahead. A 128 x 32 tile with 8 QK and 8 PV warps (registers moved by `setmaxnreg`) halves the K/V L2 traffic for long causal calls.\n- **Other head dims:** register-P tiles. P comes straight from the QK accumulator in its own key order, V rows are read in that order, and PV is computed as O^T = V^T P^T. With one CTA per SM, K/V load two blocks ahead.\n- **Planning:**\n  - The tile and launch-order model uses measured fp8 block cycles and byte counts.\n  - A decode whose packed Q rows fit 32 takes a 32-row tile.\n  - Block-sparse calls fit the tile to the sparse block over the tiles fp8 runs, with the call's paged layout.\n- **Paged KV and SplitKV:** these run the generic consumers; the DMA-warp gather writes the TMA layout. The 16-bit paged decode dataflows of #3109 pass P through SMEM in the input type, so the planner keeps fp8 off them. Paged tiles keep 16 rows per warp: with four consumer warps, 32 rows of O per warp spill from hd 128 up.\n\n## Relation to #2980\n#2980 adds an E4M3 path to the SM80-derived `flash_fwd_sm120.py`, which #3109 replaces. This PR targets the SM12x kernels instead, so the two are not stacked. Beyond #2980's stated scope, this PR adds:\n- e5m2 inputs;\n- hd 96, 192 and 192 / 128;\n- learnable sinks, softcap and score_mod / mask_mod;\n- block sparsity;\n- paged KV for every listed head dim, and per-batch SplitKV.\n\n## Performance\nfp8 vs bf16 on this branch, RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell (188 SMs):\n- **Method:** CUDA-graph replay, median of 9. The bf16 and fp8 processes ran in bf16 / fp8 / fp8 / bf16 order on the same GPU; each ratio uses the mean of its two runs. Run-to-run spread is under 6%.\n\n| | cases | fp8 speedup over bf16 |\n|---|---|---|\n| Prefill: hd 64/96/128/192/256, MHA 16/16 and GQA 32/8, S 2048 / 8192 (16K tokens), causal and full | 40 | geomean **1.69x** (1.55 to 1.93x) |\n| Prefill: hd 192 / 128, same grid | 8 | geomean **1.67x** (1.45 to 1.90x) |\n| Paged decode (q = 1, page 256, L2 flushed per call): hd 64/128/256, GQA 32/8 and 24/2, batch 8 / 64, context 4K / 32K | 24 | geomean **1.84x** (1.42 to 2.03x) |\n\nDecode at batch 64 and 32K context runs at about twice bf16's speed, matching the halved KV bytes.\n\n## Tests\n`tests/cute/test_flash_attn_sm120_fp8.py` checks O and LSE against FP32 attention on the dequantized inputs. The O bound is the upstream fp8 rule (`check_tensor_vs_ref`); LSE must be exactly -inf for rows without keys. The file covers:\n- dense shapes and both formats with descales, causal / local / full;\n- varlen / paged / SplitKV decode with NaN bytes in unused cache rows, plus an empty sequence;\n- block sparsity: dense, paged, and varlen Q over ragged paged caches;\n- one-query fixed / varlen sparse calls, and the host rejection of blocks no fp8 tile divides;\n- score_mod with a learnable sink and varlen; softcap.\n\nEvery test supports the two-pass compile / execute flow. The SM100 fp8 paged decode, partial descale and unused-V-cache tests in `test_flash_attn.py` also run on SM12x.\n\n| Run | RTX PRO 6000 |\n|---|---|\n| `test_flash_attn_sm120_fp8.py` | 114 passed |\n| two-pass (`FLASH_ATTENTION_FAKE_TENSOR=1`, then `FLASH_ATTENTION_TEST_EXPECT_CACHED=1`) | 114 / 114 |\n| `test_flash_attn_sm120.py` (with this commit) | 135 passed |\n| `test_block_sparsity.py` | 4883 passed, 40 skipped |\n| upstream fp8 tests in `test_flash_attn.py` | 12 passed |\n\nThe fp8 file also passes on DGX Spark (GB10); that run predates the last test additions.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T00:26:04Z","updated_at":"2026-11-05T08:08:12Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"81ee51e83fb0f20a771532ce5bbbefe42a3dfcbc","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"lucifer1004:pr/sm12x-fp8","ref":"pr/sm12x-fp8","repo":{"id":1436872392,"node_id":"R_kgDOVaTuyA","name":"flash-attention","full_name":"lucifer1004/flash-attention","owner":{"login":"lucifer1004","id